Here is the root cause:
The bug was caused by the lack of proper synchronization when looking up transactions, specifically the absence of a read lock, which led to inconsistencies in the handling of read and write operations. This issue was introduced in a previous commit and resulted in missing records after compacting due to broken control mechanisms for transaction management.

